Read Path — shipped data, and where it comes from.

data/glosses.tsv (the merge behind every gloss in this build)
    CC-CEDICT, its Cantonese readings, and CC-Canto, licensed Creative
    Commons Attribution-ShareAlike. The source file's own attribution notice
    is reproduced verbatim at the foot of this file, which is where the
    licence's requirement is actually discharged — the summary here is a
    convenience and carries no weight of its own.
    https://cc-canto.org/  https://cc-cedict.org/

Word frequency list (the ordering behind the learning order, and the
segmentation lexicon's corpus half)
    words.hk Word Frequency List — https://words.hk/faiman/analysis/
    "Data License: public domain. Credits to words.hk appreciated."
    Credited here, with thanks.

Character decomposition (data/ids.tsv)
    CHISE / CJKVI IDS, with BabelStone IDS as the fallback for characters
    CJKVI leaves atomic.

Formation types and stroke counts
    Wiktionary, CC-BY-SA.

NOT in this build: the words.hk dictionary dump (sources/wordshk-all.csv).
It is marked do-not-redistribute and its licence at
https://words.hk/base/hoifong/ forbids commercial use without an exemption.
features.py's `wordshk` flag is off, and tools/build_dist.py refuses to build
with it on.


